<section class="content-block white">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-title"><h1>Help</h1></div>
    <div class="infobox">
      <p>If the video does not load, use these steps. The game does not need the video.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open the training cards. There are 10 New York homes and 10 San Francisco homes, and every class uses this same pack.</li>
        <li>Build a decision tree from the five features on the cards. Run the model to see how many of the 20 cards it gets right. That percentage is the training score.</li>
        <li>Write down how confident the team is, as a percentage, before the evaluation.</li>
        <li>Evaluate the tree. A class session uses a fixed set of new homes, so the teacher can run it again in the next lesson and get the same result.</li>
      </ol>
      <div style="padding:47.14% 0 0 0;position:relative;">
        <iframe src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/893677874?h=988b2c5b98&amp;badge=0&amp;autopause=0&amp;player_id=0&amp;app_id=58479" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;" title="ML Game - Tutor's guide"></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
